# Cloudflare Pages response headers (PLAN 3.12, QUESTIONS Q10, R15). Docs:
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# - Wildcard rules only: Pages allows at most 100 rules (tests/security/headers.test.ts).
# - Every matching rule applies, in file order. A header set by two rules is JOINED with
#   ", ", so a rule that replaces a header detaches it first with "! Name".
# - The document Content-Security-Policy lives in a <meta> tag (Astro experimental.csp,
#   sha256 hashes, src/config/csp.ts). The header CSP below carries ONLY frame-ancestors:
#   both policies are enforced, so a header script-src/default-src would block the hashed
#   inline scripts. Keep it equal to HEADER_CSP in src/config/csp.ts (checked by the test).
# - HTML pages have clean URLs without an extension, so the HTML cache policy is the
#   catch-all default on /* and every asset rule below replaces it.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), serial=(), hid=(), bluetooth=(), midi=(), accelerometer=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), display-capture=(), screen-wake-lock=(), xr-spatial-tracking=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), browsing-topics=(), fullscreen=(self)
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# Vite/Astro output: content-hashed file names that never change in place.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/_astro/*.wasm
  ! Content-Type
  Content-Type: application/wasm

# Engine worker: a worker's CSP comes from its own response, not from the page's <meta>.
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' covers Chrome 97+ and Safari 16+; 'unsafe-eval' lets WASM compile on
# Chrome 90-96 (Q10). Pages joins it to the frame-ancestors policy above with ", ", which
# browsers read as a second, separately enforced policy.
/_astro/workers/*
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'unsafe-eval'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'

# pdf.js worker: parses untrusted PDFs, so no eval at all (pdfjs 5+ never needs it).
/_astro/pdf.worker*
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'

# Workbox runtime (hashed file name).
/workbox-*.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The service worker must always revalidate so updates reach users.
/sw.js
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  ! Content-Type
  Content-Type: application/manifest+json

# Self-hosted fonts (stable names, rarely change).
/fonts/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

# Generated OG images.
/og/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# Dev-only pages (not built for production; belt and braces).
/dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

# Pages project and per-deployment preview hosts must never be indexed; production runs on
# the custom domain (LAUNCH_CHECKLIST.md).
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow

https://:version.:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
